{# Widget "map" — the coverage map (PL·05), with the filter row the design puts
   on both the map and the log.

   THE MAP IS THE ATLAS'S. What is drawn on it is stated in PHP
   (Service/PatrolMap) and rendered by render_map(): the imagery, the boundary
   treatment, the control stack, the legend and fullscreen are the platform's,
   and this module writes no map JavaScript.

   The filter row goes in the plate's own filter slot, one row above the map and
   inside the plate, so the chips come along into fullscreen instead of being
   left behind on the page. Type, station and zone still drive the log and the
   lists; the map's own type filtering is the legend, which carries one
   switchable row per patrol type. #}
{% import '@UhifadhiPatrol/dashboard/_ui.html.twig' as ui %}
{% set patrolFilters %}{{ ui.filters(dashboard, types, typeColor, now, area, filter) }}{% endset %}
<div class="c">
    <span class="tab">Coverage<span class="src">· one filter drives map AND log</span></span>
    {{ render_map(map, {'role': 'img', 'aria-label': 'Patrol tracks'}, patrolFilters) }}
    <p class="patrol-note">patrol tracks may cross the boundary · a station sits where its patrols set out</p>
</div>
